Pi coding agent — example extensions
------------------------------------

Upstream:  @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent
Project:   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
Path:      packages/coding-agent/examples/extensions/
Version:   0.84.4
Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner

Redistributed as TypeScript and loaded by Pi's own runtime, so they are neither
compiled nor held to this project's compiler strictness (see tsconfig.json).
Each file carries the same provenance in its own header.

`npm run check:upstream` compares them against the examples in the installed Pi
and fails on any difference this file does not record. Without it the copies age
silently: they are not compiled, not type-checked, and the tests only prove they
load.

Byte-identical to upstream:

  extensions/upstream/preset.ts
  extensions/upstream/questionnaire.ts
  extensions/upstream/todo.ts
  extensions/upstream/tools.ts
  extensions/upstream/plan-mode/utils.ts
  extensions/upstream/subagent/agents.ts
  extensions/upstream/subagent/index.ts

Modified, and how:

  extensions/upstream/plan-mode/index.ts
      registers /plan-todos instead of /todos, because todo.ts owns /todos and
      the second registration would shadow it

Pi coding agent — example subagents and prompt templates
--------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent
Project:   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
Path:      packages/coding-agent/examples/extensions/subagent/
Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner

These arrived here through pi-setup, which records the same provenance. The
markdown carries no header of its own: a header there is text the model reads on
every use, and scout-and-plan.md could not carry one and stay byte-identical to
upstream. This file is their only record.

  prompts/scout-and-plan.md         byte-identical
  prompts/implement.md              + verification step
  prompts/implement-and-review.md   + verification step, reviewer sees the diff
  agents/planner.md                 model pin removed, handoff sentence added
  agents/scout.md                   tool limits and refusal handling rewritten
  agents/reviewer.md                output format and bash scope rewritten
  agents/worker.md                  rewritten around what a headless run can do

Everything under skills/, content/, src/, scripts/, and extensions/ outside
extensions/upstream/ is original to this repository or to pi-setup, both MIT
under LICENSE.

The npm dependencies and Pi packages named by Arcwell are separate works and
remain subject to their respective licenses and notices. They are not copied
into the Arcwell package tarball; setup asks Pi to install selected exact
